# CODEOWNERS: trust-critical path routing
#
# Sentience produces evidence. The paths below decide what an event means,
# what counts as a violation, and when enforcement fires. A quiet change to
# any of them changes what a downstream operator, reviewer, or auditor is
# looking at. They are maintainer-governed and need design agreement before
# change.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENFORCEMENT STATUS: read this before assuming a review is blocked
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "Require review from Code Owners" is NOT currently enabled as a required
# check. The practical effect of this file today is auto-requested review and
# an explicit statement of which paths need design agreement before change.
#
# What gates a merge today:
#   1. Required CI (test suite + public-surface guard)
#   2. Maintainer review against the stated acceptance criteria
#
# Only the maintainer merges into the protected branch, creates releases, or
# publishes the package.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md, "Maintainer-governed changes".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                                       @rohynal

